# Docker dev uses your real host Postgres by default (same :5432 database as local dev).
# Containers connect via host.docker.internal.

# Optional: use an isolated Postgres in Docker instead (port 5433, runs migrate deploy):
# DOCKER_USE_BUNDLED_POSTGRES=1

# Override host reachability from inside Docker (rare):
# DOCKER_DB_HOST=host.docker.internal

# Emails (@repo/mailer):
# - Auth (Express): MAILER_* in backend/.env
# - Membership (Next/tRPC): MAILER_* in root .env
# Gmail SMTP must be reachable from the container (Colima/Docker network).

# Production Docker (docker compose --profile prod up app api) requires:
# - root .env with DATABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, MAILER_* (Next membership mail)
# - backend/.env with JWT_TOKEN, MAILER_* (Express auth mail), etc.
